'.\" -*- nroff -*-
.TH KAFSRESIZE 8 "2026-07-22" "kafs 0.4.0" "System Administration"
.SH NAME
kafsresize \- grow offline KAFS images and create or populate migration images
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B kafsresize
.B --grow
.B --size-bytes
.I N
.I image
.br
.B kafsresize
.B --migrate-create
.B --dst-image
.I image
.RI [ --size-bytes " " N ]
.B --inodes
.I I
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B kafsresize
.B --migrate-create
.B --src-image
.I source
.B --dst-image
.I image
.B --format-version
.I 7
.B --inodes
.I I
.RI [ --dry-run ]
.RI [ options ]
.br
.B kafsresize
.B --migrate-import-v7
.B --src-image
.I source-v5
.B --dst-image
.I destination-v7
.RI [ --size-bytes " " N ]
.RI [ --inodes " " I ]
.RI [ --json ]
.RI [ options ]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B kafsresize
performs offline image growth within preallocated headroom and can also create
a migration target image with new geometry for cutover workflows.

It also supports creating a migration target image with new geometry
(size/inode count) via
.B --migrate-create
for cutover workflows.

The three operation modes are mutually exclusive. Options are accepted only
by the modes that list them below. Missing option values, malformed numeric
values, unknown options, extra operands, and mode-inapplicable options are
rejected with exit status 2 before an image is opened or created.
Prefix a path value that begins with a hyphen with
.BR ./ .

.B --migrate-import-v7
builds a new format-v7 image directly from a frozen format-v5 regular-file
image. The offline importer preserves inode numbers, directories, regular-file
hardlinks, symlink payloads, permissions, uid/gid, timestamps, and dense file
payloads. It does not route writes through the v5/v6 runtime or the bounded v7
FUSE write surface.

The importer validates the source namespace and representation before writing,
constructs a private
.IB destination-v7 .kafs-import-partial
work image, validates the complete v7 layout, and publishes the requested final
path only after validation. On an interrupted or rejected import before the
publication link, the final path is absent and an existing partial work image
is preserved for diagnosis. If publication directory sync or its rollback
fails after linking, the command fails and reports that both paths require
inspection.
After the final path itself is durably published, a failure to remove or sync
the redundant work-image name is reported as a warning without invalidating
the final image.
Special files, sparse payloads, pending block references, inconsistent
namespace/link state, insufficient destination geometry, and an existing final
or work path are rejected. This command does not perform cutover.

When
.B --src-mount
and
.B --dst-mount
are provided, the suggested cutover workflow prints an initial seed
copy plus a final rsync command using
.B --inplace --no-whole-file
to reduce re-transfer and rewrite volume before the final switch.

Current v0 implementation is conservative and supports growth only within
preallocated headroom:

- current logical block count: `s_blkcnt`
- maximum bitmap-backed block count: `s_r_blkcnt`

`kafsresize` can grow only when `s_blkcnt < s_r_blkcnt` and target blocks do not exceed `s_r_blkcnt`.
It updates block bitmap bits for the newly exposed range and increments `s_blkcnt_free`.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B --grow
Enable grow operation (shrink is not supported).
.TP
.B --migrate-create
Create a new destination image for migration using
.BR mkfs.kafs (8)
with inode count and target size.
When
.B --size-bytes
is omitted, size is auto-detected from
.B --dst-image
(block device capacity on Linux, or regular file size).
.TP
.B --dry-run
Validate migration-create inputs without writing
.BR --dst-image .
For
.B --format-version 7
this requires
.B --src-image
and checks that the source is a clean v5 image, that destination inode and data
capacity can hold the currently used source counts, and that the selected
descriptor-backed layout is valid.
.br
For
.BR --migrate-import-v7 ,
dry-run performs the full read-only source and exact destination-capacity
preflight but creates neither the work image nor the final destination.
This option does not apply to
.BR --grow .
.TP
.B --migrate-import-v7
Import a frozen, clean format-v5 regular-file image into a new format-v7 image.
The final destination must not exist; this mode does not accept
.BR --force .
.TP
.B --json
For
.BR --migrate-import-v7
only, replace the normal human success summary with one
.B KAFS.V5V7MigrationImportResult.v1
JSON object on standard output.  The object records PASS or FAIL, the exit
status, dry-run or import mode, source and destination paths, a typed result
object on success (or null on execution failure), and non-authorization
claims.  Diagnostics remain on standard error.  Command-line errors exit 2
before a JSON result is emitted.
.TP
.B --src-image image
Source image used by
migration precheck. For
.BR --migrate-create ,
it applies only with
.B --format-version 7
and is required by that format. The source is validated before the destination
image is overwritten.
For
.BR --migrate-import-v7 ,
it must be an unmounted, clean, dense, representable format-v5 regular-file
image and remains opened read-only. Its identity and whole-image CRC32 are
checked again before destination publication.
.TP
.B --size-bytes N
Target logical size in bytes (supports `K/M/G` suffixes).
For
.BR --migrate-create ,
this is optional and defaults to auto-detect from
.BR --dst-image .
For
.BR --migrate-import-v7 ,
it defaults to the source image byte size.
.TP
.B --dst-image image
Destination image path used by
.BR --migrate-create
or
.BR --migrate-import-v7 .
.TP
.B --inodes I
Destination inode count for
.BR --migrate-create .
For
.BR --migrate-import-v7 ,
it defaults to the source inode count and may not be smaller.
.TP
.B --format-version V
Optional on-disk format version forwarded to
.BR mkfs.kafs .
This allows
.B --migrate-create
to select the destination image format explicitly.
When omitted, the destination image follows the current
.BR mkfs.kafs
default (v5).
Use
.BR --format-version 4
to keep a legacy v4 destination image.
Use
.BR --format-version 7
with
.B --src-image
to run the same source and capacity precheck using the accepted v7 group-local
layout planner before creating a destination accepted by
.BR kafsdump (8),
.BR fsck.kafs (8),
and the v7 inspection runtime.
For
.BR --migrate-import-v7 ,
version 7 is implicit; any explicit value other than 7 is rejected.
.TP
.B --journal-size-bytes N
Optional journal size forwarded to
.BR mkfs.kafs .
.TP
.B --blksize-log L
Optional log2 block size forwarded to
.BR mkfs.kafs .
The accepted CLI range is 1 through 31.
For
.BR --migrate-import-v7 ,
it defaults to the source block size.
.TP
.B --hrl-entry-ratio R
Optional HRL entry ratio forwarded to
.BR mkfs.kafs .
Valid range is greater than 0 and less than or equal to 1.0.
.TP
.B --v7-group-count N
Optional destination group count for
.BR --migrate-import-v7 .
When omitted, the v7 layout planner selects the group count.
.TP
.B --src-mount PATH
Optional source mount path; printed in suggested rsync commands.
.TP
.B --dst-mount PATH
Optional destination mount path; printed in suggested mount/rsync commands,
including a final low-transfer rsync step.
.TP
.B --yes
Skip confirmation prompt for
.BR --migrate-create .
.TP
.B --force
Overwrite existing destination image for
.BR --migrate-create .
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Resize succeeded.
.TP
.B 1
Runtime I/O, bounds, unsupported-headroom, or migration execution error after
the command line has passed validation.
.TP
.B 2
Command-line contract error, including malformed or mode-inapplicable input.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR kafs (1),
.BR kafsctl (1),
.BR mkfs.kafs (8),
.BR fsck.kafs (8),
.BR kafsimage (8),
.BR kafsdump (8),
.BR kafs-info (8)
.SH AUTHOR
kafs project.
